NAME
    esde-check - load and measure ES-DE themes as TSV

SYNOPSIS
    esde-check [--diagnostics | --properties] [--systems a,b,...]
               <folder>...

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.dev module wrapping the check module of
    emusen-esde (Frontend/esde). Each <folder> may be either a single
    ES-DE theme (containing capabilities.xml directly or in its first
    subdirectory) or a corpus directory whose subdirectories are themes.

    Each theme is loaded once per selectable variant (or once when no
    variant is offered) and per system at 1280x800 with automatic layout
    choices. By default the five core systems are tested: nes, snes, gb,
    gbc, and n64. Nothing is downloaded; themes must already exist on
    disk.

    Output is tab-separated values with a header row. Default summary
    mode prints one row per theme:

        theme        Theme folder name.
        loads        'yes' if every requested system is themed by some
                     variant.
        systems      Number of requested systems themed.
        variants     Selectable variants (1 if none declared).
        runs         Total loads performed (variants * systems).
        errors       Total errors across runs (each unthemes a system).
        warnings     Total warnings across runs.
        set          Distinct type.property pairs set across runs.
        unknown      Pairs unrecognized by the loader (errors).
        unsupported  Pairs recognized but not drawn by the painter.
        whole        'yes' when loaded with no unknown or unsupported
                     properties and no undrawn element kinds.
        kinds        Element kinds used by the theme.
        undrawn      Kinds not drawn (and carousel:<type> for partially
                     drawn wheel carousels).

    A trailing comment line summarizes totals across the run:
    '# N themes, N load, N drawn whole, N use no undrawn kind'.

OPTIONS
    --diagnostics
        Print one TSV row per distinct warning or error instead of the
        summary table: theme, severity, code, file (relative to the
        theme), line, and message.
    --properties
        Print one TSV row per property pair: theme, type.property, and
        state ('set', 'unsupported', or 'unknown') against the scene
        mapping table (Frontend/esde/src/scene/mapping.tsv).
    --systems a,b,...
        Comma-separated list of system short names to test instead of
        the default five.

EXAMPLES
    esde-check ~/.cache/emusen/bigpicture/corpus/xml
    esde-check --diagnostics ~/.cache/emusen/bigpicture/corpus/xml/caralt-es-de
    esde-check --properties --systems snes ~/themes/art-book-next-es-de

EXIT STATUS
    0   Every theme loaded cleanly.
    1   One or more themes failed to load.
    2   Invalid options, missing folder argument, or folder not found.

SEE ALSO
    theme-check(1), qml-rules(1), dupes(1)
